            "text": "{\"primary_meaning\":\"Sin, hypocrisy, false teaching, and corruption that spreads pervasively and contaminates the whole.\",\"primary_basis\":[\"1 Corinthians 5:6-8\",\"Matthew 16:6-12\",\"Galatians 5:9\",\"Luke 12:1\",\"Exodus 12:15-20\"],\"alternatives\":[{\"meaning\":\"The Kingdom of God, representing the hidden, pervasive, and transformative growth of the gospel and grace in the world.\",\"basis\":[\"Matthew 13:33\",\"Luke 13:20-21\"],\"prominence\":\"common\"},{\"meaning\":\"A universally negative corrupting influence, arguing that even in the Parable of the Leaven it represents false doctrine or apostasy secretly entering the visible church rather than the gospel's positive growth.\",\"basis\":[\"Matthew 13:33\",\"Leviticus 2:11\"],\"prominence\":\"minority\"}],\"has_settled_consensus\":true,\"confidence\":\"high\",\"notes\":\"Leaven is overwhelmingly used as a negative symbol for sin and false doctrine in both testaments, primarily based on the Feast of Unleavened Bread and apostolic warnings. However, the Parable of the Leaven introduces a highly recognized, positive alternative meaning regarding the growth of the Kingdom of Heaven, leading to a recognized duality in its symbolic usage.\"}",
